s","skos:altLabel":["Alcohol use (LGBTQ)","Alcohol use in LGBTQ+ communities","Drug use (LGBTQ)","Drug use in LGBTQ+ communities","LGBTQ+ substance use","Substance use (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"The use of substances (that are typically deemed harmful or are subject to legal restriction, such as drugs or alcohol) and discussions surrounding the particular impact of substance use within LGBTQ+ communities.","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001550","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001007","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001125","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001235","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001549","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002226","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002229"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000380"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/drugs"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000291","dc:identifier":"homoit0000291","skos:prefLabel":"Cocaine","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001235","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002226","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85027558"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000380"},"dc:isReplacedBy":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000380"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/cocaine"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-08-22"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000292","dc:identifier":"homoit0000292","skos:prefLabel":"Cock rings","rdfs:comment":"Rings or circular sex toys worn on the penis to maintain an erection and prevent orgasm.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001266","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001099","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001266"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/cockRings"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000293","dc:identifier":"homoit0000293","skos:prefLabel":"Enemas","skos:altLabel":"Colonic irrigation","rdfs:comment":"A liquid application device used as a douche or to cleanse the bowels or vagina, or usage of such a device. Can be used for sexual or erotic purposes.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000442","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001266","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001267","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001299","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003059"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000076","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000081","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003124"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85043118"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000404"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/enemas"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000294","dc:identifier":"homoit0000294","skos:prefLabel":"Collars","rdfs:comment":"Straps or bands of material worn around the neck. May be worn as a fashion statement, to signal \"ownership\" by a dominant partner within the context of a BDSM relationship, or during sex to restrict the wearer's movement and breath control.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001266","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000214","skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85027979"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001266"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/collars"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000295","dc:identifier":"homoit0000295","skos:prefLabel":"Coming out","rdfs:comment":"Process of accepting and sharing one’s sexual or gender identity with oneself and/or others.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000088","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000089","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000285","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000286","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000287","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000288","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001065","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001261","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001783","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001784","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001785","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001786","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001787","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002905","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003509"],"skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh90005890"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000295"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/comingOut"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000296","dc:identifier":"homoit0000296","skos:prefLabel":"Common law marriage","rdfs:comment":"Legal framework in which two partners are considered married without having formally registered their relationship as a civil or religious marriage. Common law marriage grants certain economic rights and legal privileges. ","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000990","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000992"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85028995"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000973"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/commonLawMarriage"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000298","dc:identifier":"homoit0000298","skos:prefLabel":["LGBTQ+ community centers","LGBTQ+ community centres"],"rdfs:comment":"Spaces in which people from LGBTQ+ communities meet for social, education, recreational, or organizing activities. ","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000830","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000900"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000144","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000486","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000734","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001171","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001404","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001512","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002775","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002968"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000297","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002689"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2021008660"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000830"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/communityCentresLGBTQ"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000299","dc:identifier":"homoit0000299","skos:prefLabel":"Condoms","skos:altLabel":["Prophylactics","Rubbers"],"rdfs:comment":"Latex contraceptives used to cover penises during sexual activity for the purposes of preventing STIs and/or pregnancy.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001266","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001251","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85030795"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001266"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/condoms"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000300","dc:identifier":"homoit0000300","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ Confucianists","skos:altLabel":["Confucianists (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ Confucianists"],"rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people who are Confucianists.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000928","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000928"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/LGBTQConfucianists"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000301","dc:identifier":"homoit0000301","skos:prefLabel":"Congenital adrenal hyperplasia","skos:altLabel":"CAH","rdfs:comment":"Congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH) is a group of different but related genetic variations that affect the enzymes that allow the adrenal glands to make hormones that regulate the body’s functions. People with CAH do not consistently produce the amount of cortisol or aldosterone they need, but they may naturally produce higher-than-typical levels of androgens such as testosterone to help the body compensate. Someone with CAH can be born with XX or XY chromosomes. People with CAH and XY chromosomes are usually not considered to have a variation in sex characteristics since an increased amount of androgens will not cause the development of any characteristics that are not considered typical for people assigned male at birth. In people with XX chromosomes and CAH, the increase in androgen production can result in genital differences such as a larger-than-typical clitoris, fused labia, and the fusion of the urethra and vaginal canal to form a single opening. They may also develop some characteristics like body and facial hair or increased muscle mass during childhood or puberty.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000669","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002827","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002869"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85001014"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/congenitalAdrenalHyperplasia"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303","dc:identifier":"homoit0000303","skos:prefLabel":"Conversion therapy","skos:altLabel":["Reparative therapy","Reorientation therapy","Sexual reorientation therapy"],"rdfs:comment":"Efforts to change the sexual or gender identity of an individual who is or is suspected to be LGBTQ+ to meet heterosexual or cisgender norms, typically under the belief that being LGBTQ+ is dangerous and/or the result of mental illness or trauma. The processes involved in conversion therapy include visualization training, spiritual interventions, and other aversion treatments. ","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000106","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003512","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006004076"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/sexualReorientation"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000304","dc:identifier":"homoit0000304","skos:prefLabel":"Second parent adoption","skos:altLabel":"Co-parent adoption","rdfs:comment":"An adoption process by which a legal child-parent relationship is established by granting the “second” parent the same rights as the “first” parent without the “first” or legal parent relinquishing any parental rights. A second or co-parent adoption can be important for LGBTQ+ parents to protect their parental rights as the relationship of the non-biological parent may not be recognized in some jurisdictions without such an adoption.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000809","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000918","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000864"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/secondParentAdoption"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000305","dc:identifier":"homoit0000305","skos:prefLabel":"Scat play","skos:altLabel":["Coprophilia","Coprolagnia","Extrementophilia","Fecalphilia","Fecophilia","Poop fetish","Poop fetishism","Poop kink","Scat fetish","Scat fetishism","Scat kink","Scat","Scatophilia"],"rdfs:comment":"Use of feces for erotic enjoyment.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000442","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000081","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000597"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2019000046"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000404"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/scat"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000306","dc:identifier":"homoit0000306","skos:prefLabel":"Corrective rape","rdfs:comment":"Criminal practice in which men rape lesbians, sometimes under the supervision of members of the women's families or local communities, with the purported purpose of \"curing\" them of homosexuality.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001305","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000783","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000793","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003444"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001305"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/correctiveRape"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001305","dc:identifier":"homoit0001305","skos:prefLabel":"Sexual violence","rdfs:comment":"Sexual acts or attempts to coerce sexual acts that involve the use of non-consensual violence. This term encompasses sexual assault, rape, and sexual abuse.","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000306","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000855","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000938","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000958","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001285","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003433"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000059","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002195","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003444"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85120572"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001305"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/sexualViolence"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000307","dc:identifier":"homoit0000307","skos:prefLabel":"Corsets","skos:altLabel":["Bondage corsets","Tightlacing"],"rdfs:comment":"A garment worn to hold and train the torso into a desired shape, traditionally a smaller waist or larger bottom, for aesthetic purposes (either for the duration of wearing it or with a more lasting effect), or to support the breasts.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003059","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003066"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003076","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003113"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85033068"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000404"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/corsets"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000308","dc:identifier":"homoit0000308","skos:prefLabel":"Cottages (Gay culture)","skos:altLabel":["Public urinals","Cottages"],"rdfs:comment":"UK slang term for public bathrooms used as locations for sexual encounters, particularly by gay men.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000974","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000595","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000309","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001140","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001358"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000974"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/cottages"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000309","dc:identifier":"homoit0000309","skos:prefLabel":"Cottaging (Gay culture)","skos:altLabel":"Cottaging","rdfs:comment":"UK slang term commonly used in gay communities to describe the practice of engaging in anonymous sex in a public bathroom or cruising for sexual partners there. ","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001267","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001299"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000050","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000308","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000319","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001142","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001357"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001267"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/cottaging"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000310","dc:identifier":"homoit0000310","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ couples","skos:altLabel":"Couples (LGBTQ)","rdfs:comment":"Partnerships in which both people are LGBTQ+.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001237","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000145","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000218","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000503","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000735","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001172","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001405","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002780","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002969"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001083","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002690"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001237"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/couplesLGBTQ"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000311","dc:identifier":"homoit0000311","skos:prefLabel":"Court orders","rdfs:comment":"Proclamations by a judge or panel of judges requiring or authorizing specific actions (e.g., court orders approving or denying requests for name or gender marker changes).","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000702","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001053"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000119","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000377","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000573"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000702"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/courtOrders"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000312","dc:identifier":"homoit0000312","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ victims of crime","skos:altLabel":["Crime victims (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ victims of crime"],"rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people who have experienced crimes and may or may not have survived; follow the individual's preference for “victims” or “survivors” whenever possible.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000613","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000958","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000959","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003745"],"skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001492","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/LGBTQVictimsOfCrime"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000313","dc:identifier":"homoit0000313","skos:prefLabel":"Criminal law","rdfs:comment":"Body of law relating to crime that prescribes the legality and consequences of conduct perceived as threatening, harmful, or endangering to the property, health, safety, and/or moral welfare of oneself and others. ","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000702","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000314","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000339","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001289"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85034058"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000702"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/criminalLaw"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000314","dc:identifier":"homoit0000314","skos:prefLabel":["Criminalization","Criminalisation"],"rdfs:comment":"The process by which behaviors and individuals are framed as and come to be known as criminal.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000313","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002379","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002388","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003773"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000339","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001139","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003499"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000702"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/criminalisation"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000315","dc:identifier":"homoit0000315","skos:prefLabel":"Cross-cultural relationships","skos:altLabel":["Intercultural relationships","Interracial relationships"],"rdfs:comment":"Relationships between people of different ethnic or racial backgrounds.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001237","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001295","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001636"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001237"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/cross-culturalRelationships"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000316","dc:identifier":"homoit0000316","skos:prefLabel":"Crossdressers","skos:altLabel":"Cross-dressers","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who wear clothes stereotypical to or associated with a gender other than their predominantly-identified gender. Crossdressers often develop a persona while crossdressing. Only use to describe individuals who self-identify as crossdressers.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001817","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000289","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000318","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000373","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000375","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000396","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000970","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001076","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001085","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001090","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001470","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001781"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh89002495"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001817"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/crossdressers"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001817","dc:identifier":"homoit0001817","skos:prefLabel":"Gender minorities","skos:altLabel":["Gender variance","Gender variant people","Non-normative genders"],"rdfs:comment":"Individuals whose gender identities and practices differ from those of the dominant culture. Use the term \"Sexual minorities\" for individuals whose sexual identities, orientations, and practices differ from those of the dominant culture.","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000021","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000045","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000316","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000342","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000570","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000574","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000582","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001072","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001470","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001474","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001668"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000560","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000566","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000571","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000577","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000581","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001297","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit000181