12-18 years of age, also known as young adult literature or YA; use in reference to youth literature focusing on transgender characters or themes.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001522","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001452","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transgenderYouthLiterature"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001463","dc:identifier":"homoit0001463","skos:prefLabel":"Transgenderism","rdfs:comment":"Pathologizing term often used in the medicalization of transgender people; use only in historical contexts.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001006","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001468","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000395","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000560","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000571","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000805","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001409","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001423","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001447","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001563"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transgenderism"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001464","dc:identifier":"homoit0001464","skos:prefLabel":"Transitioning status","rdfs:comment":"Term used to describe a person’s current status in their gender transition.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001047","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001049","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001129","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001131"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000561","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001381","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001834","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001835","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001836","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001837","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001838","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001839"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001465"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transitioningStatus"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001466","dc:identifier":"homoit0001466","skos:prefLabel":"Transmasculine people","rdfs:comment":"Trans people assigned female at birth who identify partially or fully with a masculine gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000215","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000995","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001653","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001820","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002061"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transmasculinePeople"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001467","dc:identifier":"homoit0001467","skos:prefLabel":"Transphobia","rdfs:comment":"Antagonism or disgust directed toward trans individuals (or others perceived to be transgressing gender norms) due to their gender identity and/or expression. Transphobia can include denial of the existence of trans identities, stereotypes, verbal harassment, and physical violence.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000920","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002212","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002593","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003158"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000062","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000063","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000619","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001819","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001892","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001903","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003499","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003737"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010012303"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000920"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transphobia"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001468","dc:identifier":"homoit0001468","skos:prefLabel":"Transsexualism","rdfs:comment":"An individual's identification with a gender inconsistent with or not culturally associated with their assigned sex.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001006","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001463"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000395","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001380","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001381","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001496","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001563"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh94005829"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transsexualism"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001469","dc:identifier":"homoit0001469","skos:prefLabel":"Transvestism","rdfs:comment":"U.S. historical term used to describe the practices of individuals who wear clothes associated with a gender other than their gender assigned at birth; generally considered to be a derogatory term; use only in historical contexts.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001006"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000318","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000395","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001563","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001895"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transvestism"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001470","dc:identifier":"homoit0001470","skos:prefLabel":"Transvestites","rdfs:comment":"U.S. historical term used to describe individuals who wear clothes associated with a gender other than their gender assigned at birth; generally considered to be a derogatory term; use only in historical contexts.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001817"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000316","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001781"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000878"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/transvestites"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001471","dc:identifier":"homoit0001471","skos:prefLabel":"Travestis","skos:altLabel":"Travesti","rdfs:comment":"Spanish term for people assigned male at birth who have a feminine gender identity; commonly used in South America.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/travesti"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001472","dc:identifier":"homoit0001472","skos:prefLabel":"Tribades","rdfs:comment":"Historical term for individuals who engage in the sexual practice of tribadism; use only in historical contexts.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000556","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001669"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000878"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/tribades"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001473","dc:identifier":"homoit0001473","skos:prefLabel":"Trigender identity","rdfs:comment":"Gender identity including three genders, typically male, female, and a third (often non-binary) gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000571","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001474","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/trigenderIdentity"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001474","dc:identifier":"homoit0001474","skos:prefLabel":"Trigender people","rdfs:comment":"People whose gender continually moves between or among three gender identities, typically male, female, and a third gender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001817"],"skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001473","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/trigenderPeople"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001475","dc:identifier":"homoit0001475","skos:prefLabel":"Tritiya-Prakriti","rdfs:comment":"Ancient Hindu term for a third gender that is typically described as fluid and/or continuously transformative.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/tritiyaPrakriti"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001476","dc:identifier":"homoit0001476","skos:prefLabel":"Tucking (Phallus)","skos:altLabel":"Tucking","rdfs:comment":"Slang term describing various methods used to visually conceal the penis to give a flatter appearance in clothing.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001099","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/tucking"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477","dc:identifier":"homoit0001477","skos:prefLabel":"Tumtum","rdfs:comment":"Term originating in Rabbinic Judaism to refer to someone with an unknown sex; literally translates to \"hidden.\" Used historically to refer to intersex variations where the genitals were covered by skin. Only use for individuals who are Jewish and who self-identify as Tumtum.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/tumtum"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001478","dc:identifier":"homoit0001478","skos:prefLabel":"Turner syndrome","rdfs:comment":"Turner syndrome is a variation in which a person is born with a 45X chromosome pattern (sometimes called 45XO) rather than the typical 46XX. People with Turner syndrome often share specific physical features such as short stature, a webbed neck and broad chest, and heart issues. They can also develop variations in their other sex characteristics, such as smaller-than-typical ovaries that may stop producing hormones at a younger age than typical, and they might not menstruate or experience pubertal changes.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000669","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85138930"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/turnerSyndrome"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001479","dc:identifier":"homoit0001479","skos:prefLabel":"Twinks (Gay culture)","skos:altLabel":["Twinkies","Twinks"],"rdfs:comment":"U.S. slang term for young gay men who are typically small in stature, hairless, and considered effeminate.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000506","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000577","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001295"],"skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/twinks"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001480","dc:identifier":"homoit0001480","skos:prefLabel":"Two-Spirit people","skos:altLabel":["2S people","Two Spirit people","Two Spirited people","Two-Spirited people"],"rdfs:comment":"Indigenous people in North America who self-identify as Two-Spirit to reconnect with the multiple gender and sexual roles in Native cultures.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001297"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001750","https://homosauru