ecognize their queer identity as salient to their Indigenous identity and vice versa; some but not all Indigiqueer people also identify as Two-Spirit; only use to describe individuals who self-identify as Indigiqueer.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000886","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001195"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000002","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000676","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000913","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001037","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001480","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001810"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-19"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001810","dc:identifier":"homoit0001810","skos:prefLabel":"Indigiqueer","rdfs:comment":"Term used to describe the identity of people who are both Indigenous and queer and view those identities as inherently related and interconnected.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000002","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000676","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000898","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000913","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001037","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001480","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001809"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-19"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001811","dc:identifier":"homoit0001811","skos:prefLabel":"Two-Spirit community","skos:altLabel":["2S community","Two Spirit community","Two Spirited community","Two-Spirited community"],"rdfs:comment":"A group of Two-Spirit people united by their shared identity.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000297","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001480","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002689"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001811"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-19"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001812","dc:identifier":"homoit0001812","skos:prefLabel":"Pacific Islander American LGBTQ+ people","skos:altLabel":["AAPI LGBTQ+ people","LGBTQ+ AAPIs","LGBTQ+ Pacific Islander American people","LGBTQ+ Pacific Islander Americans","Pacific Islander American people (LGBTQ)","Pacific Islander Americans (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people who identify as both Pacific Islanders (or of Pacific Islander ancestry) and American.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000860","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001101","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000886"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001937","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001938","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001939","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001940","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001941","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001942","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002926","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003423"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001813","dc:identifier":"homoit0001813","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ special collections","skos:altLabel":["Hidden collections (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ+ hidden collections","Special collections (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Special collections that hold materials primarily pertaining to LGBTQ+ people or intended for use by LGBTQ+ people. Special collections tend to be a blend of institutional types (e.g., an archives with a museum component). This term should be applied to institutions that refer to themselves as special collections; otherwise, use the term \"LGBTQ+ cultural heritage institutions.\"","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001755","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000968","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001030","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001363","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003547"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001755"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001814","dc:identifier":"homoit0001814","skos:prefLabel":"Chasers","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who express fetishistic interest in and pursue sexual encounters with others based solely on their affiliation with a (typically marginalized) group that the chaser does not belong to. Often coupled with other terms to identify the type of chaser.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000442","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001300"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000404"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001815","dc:identifier":"homoit0001815","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ immigrants","skos:altLabel":"Immigrants (LGBTQ)","rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people who have moved to another country.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000883","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000902","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000927","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001053","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001092","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001482","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001853"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2020001167"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001816","dc:identifier":"homoit0001816","skos:prefLabel":"Gender transgression","rdfs:comment":"Behaviors, acts, or forms of expression that contradict or do not conform to a given culture's norms surrounding gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000560","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000562","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000577","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000581","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001817","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003066"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001818","dc:identifier":"homoit0001818","skos:prefLabel":"Trans inclusivity","skos:altLabel":["Trans affirming","Trans inclusion","Trans inclusive","Trans supportive","Trans-inclusive"],"rdfs:comment":"The practice or policy of providing equal access and support to trans people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002291","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001378","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002291"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002291","dc:identifier":"homoit0002291","skos:prefLabel":"Inclusivity","skos:altLabel":["Inclusion","Inclusive"],"rdfs:comment":"The practice or policy of providing equal access and support to groups of people who might otherwise be excluded or marginalized, such as LGBTQ+ people, people of color, disabled people, etc.","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001818","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001819"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002291"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001819","dc:identifier":"homoit0001819","skos:prefLabel":"Trans exclusivity","skos:altLabel":["Trans exclusion","Trans exclusive","Trans-exclusive"],"rdfs:comment":"The practice or policy of denying equal access and support to trans people.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000062","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002291"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001139","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001467","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001516","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003499","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003737"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000356"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001820","dc:identifier":"homoit0001820","skos:prefLabel":"Transmasculinity","rdfs:comment":"Masculine-aligned identities or practices of trans people.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000995"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001466","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001643","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001653"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001821","dc:identifier":"homoit0001821","skos:prefLabel":"Transfemininity","rdfs:comment":"Feminine-aligned identities or practices of trans people.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000389","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001382","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001642","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001652"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001822","dc:identifier":"homoit0001822","skos:prefLabel":"Hermaphrodites","rdfs:comment":"A term originating from Greek mythology that refers to beings that are both fully female and fully male. The term was once adopted in the medical realm to describe people with intersex variations generally (and later to describe someone with both ovarian and testicular tissue specifically), but it is now recognized to be stigmatizing, imprecise, and misleading. Many people in the intersex community consider the use of this term to be pathologizing and deeply offensive, while other intersex people have chosen to reclaim the term to describe themselves and their bodies. Do not use this term to describe an individual unless they explicitly identify with it and have chosen to use it.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000352","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000618"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000878"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823","dc:identifier":"homoit0001823","skos:prefLabel":"Alloromantic people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who experience romantic attraction or desire in a frequent and consistent manner, often alongside sexual attraction.","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001824","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001825","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001826","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001827"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000067","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001791"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001824","dc:identifier":"homoit0001824","skos:prefLabel":"Biromantic people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who experience romantic attraction or desire in a frequent and consistent manner toward people of more than one sex or gender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001823","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001829"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000067","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001792","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001825","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001826","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001827"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001825","dc:identifier":"homoit0001825","skos:prefLabel":"Homoromantic people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who experience romantic attraction or desire in a frequent and consistent manner toward members of the same sex or gender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001823","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001829"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000067","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001793","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001824","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001826","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001827"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001826","dc:identifier":"homoit0001826","skos:prefLabel":"Heteroromantic people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who experience romantic attraction or romantic desire in a frequent and consistent manner toward members of the opposite sex or gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001823","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000067","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001794","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001824","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001825","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001827"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001827","dc:identifier":"homoit0001827","skos:prefLabel":"Panromantic people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who experience romantic attraction or romantic desire toward others in a frequent and consistent manner irrespective of sex or gender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001823","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001829"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000067","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001795","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001824","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001825","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001826"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001823"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001831","dc:identifier":"homoit0001831","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ culture","rdfs:comment":"Cultural experiences shared by members of LGBTQ+ communities or products of LGBTQ+ culture (e.g., art and media created by and for LGBTQ+ culture, activism focused on LGBTQ+ issues, slang commonly used in LGBTQ+ communities, etc.). Use a more specific term if possible.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001345","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000382","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000816","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000972","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001406","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001832","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001833","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002788","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002970"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001755","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003698"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001832","dc:identifier":"homoit0001832","skos:prefLabel":"Queer culture","rdfs:comment":"Cultural experiences shared by members of queer communities or products of queer culture (e.g., art and media created by and for queer people, activism focused on queer issues, slang commonly used in queer communities, etc.).","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001831","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002588","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000382","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001406","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001833"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001833","dc:identifier":"homoit0001833","skos:prefLabel":"Bisexual culture","rdfs:comment":"Use to describe cultural experiences shared by members of bisexual communities or products of bisexual culture (e.g., art and media created by and for bisexual people, activism focused on bisexual issues, slang commonly used in bisexual communities, etc.).","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001831","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000382","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001406","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001832"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001834","dc:identifier":"homoit0001834","skos:prefLabel":"Detransitioning","skos:altLabel":"Detransition","rdfs:comment":"Ceasing or reversing the process of gender transition for any reason, including personal safety, stigma, costs associated with transitioning, health concerns, to regain fertility, etc.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001835","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001836"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001465"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001835","dc:identifier":"homoit0001835","skos:prefLabel":"Retransitioning","skos:altLabel":"Retransition","rdfs:comment":"Restarting the process of gender transition after a period of detransitioning.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001834","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001836"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001465"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001836","dc:identifier":"homoit0001836","skos:prefLabel":"Desistance (Gender)","rdfs:comment":"No longer identifying as transgender, or, more broadly, no longer identifying as some particular gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001834","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001835"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001465"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001837","dc:identifier":"homoit0001837","skos:prefLabel":"Facial gender affirming surgery","skos:altLabel":["Facial gender affirmation surgery","Facial gender confirmation surgery","Facial gender confirming surgery"],"rdfs:comment":"Any of various surgeries that involve modifying the face or facial features to affirm the patient's gender.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000561","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001838","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001839"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001849"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001838","dc:identifier":"homoit0001838","skos:prefLabel":["Facial masculinization surgery","Facial masculinisation surgery"],"skos:altLabel":"FMS","rdfs:comment":"Any of various surgeries undertaken to masculinize the face or facial features.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001837","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001839"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001839","dc:identifier":"homoit0001839","skos:prefLabel":["Facial feminization surgery","Facial feminisation surgery"],"skos:altLabel":"FFS","rdfs:comment":"Any of various surgeries undertaken to feminize the face or facial features.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001837","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001849","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001464","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001838"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001840","dc:identifier":"homoit0001840","skos:prefLabel":"Top surgery","rdfs:comment":"Colloquial term for gender-affirming surgical alterations of the chest.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000561","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001620","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001631","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001841"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000114","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000584","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001841","dc:identifier":"homoit0001841","skos:prefLabel":"Chest reconstruction surgery","skos:altLabel":"Chest wall reconstruction","rdfs:comment":"Reconstruction of the chest, typically following a mastectomy, to give the chest a more masculine appearance.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001840","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001631","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003118"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001842","dc:identifier":"homoit0001842","skos:prefLabel":"Feminizing vocal surgery","skos:altLabel":["VFS","Vocal feminization surgery","Voice feminization surgery"],"rdfs:comment":"Any of various surgical procedures undertaken to feminize the voice.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000561","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001465","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001495","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001496","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001843"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-02-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001843","dc:identifier":"homoit0001843","skos:prefLabel":"Masculinizing vocal surgery","skos:altLabel":["Masculinization laryngoplasty","Vocal masculinization surgery","Voice masculinization surgery"],"rdfs:comment":"Any of various surgical procedures undertaken to masculinize the voice.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000561","s