 people who belong to the indigenous Kalasha people and reside in the Chitral District of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa province in Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002247","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-07-28"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002252","dc:identifier":"homoit0002252","skos:prefLabel":"Kalash queer people","skos:altLabel":["Queer Kalash people","Queer Kalasha"],"rdfs:comment":"Queer people who belong to the indigenous Kalasha people and reside in the Chitral District of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa province in Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002247","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-07-28"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002253","dc:identifier":"homoit0002253","skos:prefLabel":"Kalash intersex people","skos:altLabel":["Intersex Kalash people","Intersex Kalasha"],"rdfs:comment":"Intersex people who belong to the indigenous Kalasha people and reside in the Chitral District of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa province in Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002247","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-07-28"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002254","dc:identifier":"homoit0002254","skos:prefLabel":"Kalash asexual people","skos:altLabel":["Asexual Kalash people","Asexual Kalasha"],"rdfs:comment":"Asexual people who belong to the indigenous Kalasha people and reside in the Chitral District of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa province in Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002247","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-07-28"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002255","dc:identifier":"homoit0002255","skos:prefLabel":"Polygamous people","rdfs:comment":"Individuals who engage in relationships in which the dominant partner has multiple spouses, though the marriages are not typically recognized by society or law.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001637","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001081","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001123","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001124","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001629","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001659"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001637"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-09-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002256","dc:identifier":"homoit0002256","skos:prefLabel":"Gender euphoria","rdfs:comment":"The powerful feeling of joy and comfort an individual experiences when their assigned gender, gender expression, and/or the way their gender is perceived by themselves and others aligns with their gender identity. Though gender euphoria is often associated with trans people, people of any identity may experience gender euphoria when they feel that their gender has been seen and affirmed, or when they feel \"right\" in their body and the way their gender is being expressed.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000120","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000567","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000568","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000571","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002699","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002700","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003193","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003708"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002256"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-09-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002257","dc:identifier":"homoit0002257","skos:prefLabel":"Anti-Blackness","skos:altLabel":"Anti Blackness","rdfs:comment":"Term used to acknowledge the particularities of racism as directed toward Black people. Anti-Blackness includes the belief that Black people possess different inherent behavioral traits that correspond to inherited attributes and are inferior to those of other races--particularly white people. Anti-Blackness also encompasses prejudice, discrimination, and antagonism (whether personal or systematic) directed toward Black people because of their race and its perceived inferiority.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001902","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001903","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001904","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002376","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003691","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003692"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002038"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-09-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002258","dc:identifier":"homoit0002258","skos:prefLabel":"AIDS death and dying","rdfs:comment":"Experiences related to people with AIDS approaching or having reached the end of their lives.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000848","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000849","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000911","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001360"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002258"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002259","dc:identifier":"homoit0002259","skos:prefLabel":"Gender-neutral language","skos:altLabel":["Gender inclusive language","Gender neutral language","Gender-inclusive language"],"rdfs:comment":"Language that avoids the use of gender-specific words, either to be inclusive of nonbinary, agender, and other gender diverse peoples, or to avoid gender bias.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001016","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001135","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001278"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002259"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260","dc:identifier":"homoit0002260","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ history","skos:altLabel":["History (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ history"],"rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning LGBTQ+ people, or people who might be perceived as LGBTQ+ if they were alive today.","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002261","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002262","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002263","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002264","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002265","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002266","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002267","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002268","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002332","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002462","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002488","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002504","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002525"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000901","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001614","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001729","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001755","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002261","dc:identifier":"homoit0002261","skos:prefLabel":"Lesbian history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning lesbians, or people who might be perceived as lesbian if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002262","dc:identifier":"homoit0002262","skos:prefLabel":"Gay history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning gay men, or men who might be perceived as gay if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002263","dc:identifier":"homoit0002263","skos:prefLabel":"Bisexual history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning bisexual people, or people who might be perceived as bisexual if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002264","dc:identifier":"homoit0002264","skos:prefLabel":"Transgender history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning transgender people, or people who might be perceived as transgender if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002265","dc:identifier":"homoit0002265","skos:prefLabel":"Queer history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning queer people, or people who might be perceived as queer if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002266","dc:identifier":"homoit0002266","skos:prefLabel":"Intersex history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning intersex people, or people who might be perceived as intersex if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002267","dc:identifier":"homoit0002267","skos:prefLabel":"Asexual history","skos:altLabel":"Ace history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning asexual people, or people who might be perceived as asexual if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002268","dc:identifier":"homoit0002268","skos:prefLabel":"Non-binary history","skos:altLabel":"Nonbinary history","rdfs:comment":"Past events or accounts of the past concerning non-binary people, or people who might be perceived as non-binary if they were alive today.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002260"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002269","dc:identifier":"homoit0002269","skos:prefLabel":"Anti-racism","skos:altLabel":"Antiracism","rdfs:comment":"Umbrella term used to describe a range of ideas, policies, and political actions that are intended to actively challenge, reject, or oppose racism and racial oppression (whether personal or systemic), as well as advocate for racial equity.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001902","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007000043"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002269"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002270","dc:identifier":"homoit0002270","skos:prefLabel":"Black feminism","skos:altLabel":["Afro feminism","Afro-feminism"],"rdfs:comment":"A form of feminism that developed in response to the failures of mainstream feminist and civil rights efforts to acknowledge the ways white supremacy and the patriarchy interact to inform the particular experiences of Black women.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000667","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002272","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003170"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271","dc:identifier":"homoit0002271","skos:prefLabel":"White feminism","rdfs:comment":"Term used to describe (and criticize) forms of feminism that focus on the needs of white women at the expense of women of color.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000667","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001133","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002272"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2021008248"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272","dc:identifier":"homoit0002272","skos:prefLabel":"Womanism","skos:altLabel":"Womanist theory","rdfs:comment":"A social theory based on the history and everyday experiences of Black women. Womanism grew out of the perceived indifference of the feminist movement towards the needs of Black women, who are often excluded from the categories of \"female\" and \"femininity\" as understood by white feminists. At the core of womanism is the idea that mainstream feminism is a movement led by white women to serve white women's goals, which can be indifferent or even oppositional to the needs of Black women.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001365","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000667","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002270","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002271","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003176"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006001576"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273","dc:identifier":"homoit0002273","skos:prefLabel":"QTPOC","skos:altLabel":"Queer and trans people of color","rdfs:comment":"Acronym used to refer to queer and trans people of color as a group. Typically used to acknowledge the particularities of queer and trans people of color's experiences and the intersections of queerphobia, transphobia, and racism as directed towards queer and trans people of color.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001892","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001928","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001101"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274","dc:identifier":"homoit0002274","skos:prefLabel":"Transfeminism","skos:altLabel":"Trans feminism","rdfs:comment":"As defined by Emi Koyama, transfeminism is a movement by and for trans woman who view the liberation of trans women as essential to the liberation of all women.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000667","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001642","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001892","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003175"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275","dc:identifier":"homoit0002275","skos:prefLabel":"Third-wave feminism","skos:altLabel":"Third wave feminism","rdfs:comment":"Period of feminist political activity beginning in the early 1990s that embraced diversity and individualism in women and sought to redefine what it meant to be a feminist. The third wave is characterized by the emergence of new feminist movements and theories such as intersectionality, sex positivity, ecofeminism, transfeminism, and postmodern feminism.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003174","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008001561"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276","dc:identifier":"homoit0002276","skos:prefLabel":"Sapphic identity","skos:altLabel":"Sapphist identity","rdfs:comment":"Sexual identity or sexuality term used to describe women and, in some definitions, non-binary people who are sapphic, or attracted to women. Only use to describe individuals who describe their identity as sapphic.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001295","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002277","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001295"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277","dc:identifier":"homoit0002277","skos:prefLabel":"Sapphics","skos:altLabel":"Sapphists","rdfs:comment":"Women and, in some definitions, non-binary people of any sexual identity or sexuality who are attracted to women. Some but not all sapphics use the term \"sapphic\" to describe their sexual identity or sexuality. Only use to describe individuals who self-identify as sapphic.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001297"],"skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002276","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85117455"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278","dc:identifier":"homoit0002278","skos:prefLabel":"MLM (Men Loving Men)","skos:altLabel":["Man loving man","Men loving men"],"rdfs:comment":"Slang term used to describe men who have romantic and/or sexual relationships with other men; often used as an alternative to the term \"Men who have sex with men.\" Can be used to describe men who are exclusively or primarily interested in men, as well as men who are also interested in people of other or all genders. Only use to describe people who self-identify as MLM.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001008","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001297"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000365","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001254"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279","dc:identifier":"homoit0002279","skos:prefLabel":"WLW (Women Loving Women)","skos:altLabel":["Woman loving woman","Women loving women"],"rdfs:comment":"Slang term used to describe women who have romantic and/or sexual relationships with other women. Can be used to describe women who are exclusively or primarily interested in women, as well as women who are also interested in people of other or all genders. Only use to describe people who self-identify as WLW.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001297","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001509"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001254","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003613"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-08"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002280","dc:identifier":"homoit0002280","skos:prefLabel":"Mothers of queer people","skos:altLabel":["Moms of queer people","Queer people's moms","Queer people's mothers"],"rdfs:comment":"Individuals who assume the role of mother to a queer person or queer people; use only for individuals who self-identify as mothers.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002348","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002281","dc:identifier":"homoit0002281","skos:prefLabel":"Cisgender youth","skos:altLabel":["Cis youth","Cisgender adolescents","Cisgender teenagers","Cisgender teens"],"rdfs:comment":"Cisgender people who are between the ages of childhood and adulthood.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000271","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001520"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002282","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002283","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002284"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000271"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002282","dc:identifier":"homoit0002282","skos:prefLabel":"Cisgender children","skos:altLabel":["Cis children","Cis kids","Cisgender kids"],"rdfs:comment":"Children younger than 18 years who identify as cisgender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000255","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000271","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002281"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002283","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002284"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002283","dc:identifier":"homoit0002283","skos:prefLabel":"Cisgender boys","skos:altLabel":"Cis boys","rdfs:comment":"Boys (typically children or youth younger than 18) who are cisgender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000220","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002281","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002282"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002284","dc:identifier":"homoit0002284","skos:prefLabel":"Cisgender girls","skos:altLabel":"Cis girls","rdfs:comment":"Girls (typically children or youth younger than 18) who are cisgender.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000590","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002281","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002282"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002285","dc:identifier":"homoit0002285","skos:prefLabel":"Heterosexual children","skos:altLabel":["Heterosexual kids","Straight children","Straight kids"],"rdfs:comment":"Children younger than 18 years who identify as heterosexual.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000255","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000627","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000630"],"skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000621","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000623"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002286","dc:identifier":"homoit0002286","skos:prefLabel":"Yan daudu","rdfs:comment":"Nigerian term that directly translates to \"feminine men\" but cannot be easily understood through Euro-American understandings of gender. The term has been used to describe people who may identify variously as feminine men, gay men, both male and female (or third gender), and/or trans. While some people self-identify as yan daudu, others consider the term a slur. Only use to describe individuals who self-identify as yan daudu.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000322","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002287","dc:identifier":"homoit0002287","skos:prefLabel":["Mustaches","Moustaches"],"rdfs:comment":"Facial hair on the upper lip. Includes false or drag mustaches as well as naturally grown hair.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000605","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002288","skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85089102"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002288","dc:identifier":"homoit0002288","skos:prefLabel":"Cookie dusters","skos:altLabel":["Muff ticklers","Pussy dusters","Womb brooms"],"rdfs:comment":"Slang term for mustaches or facial hair on the upper lip, particularly that of lesbians.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002287","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000779","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002289","dc:identifier":"homoit0002289","skos:prefLabel":"Chemsex","rdfs:comment":"Sexual activities that include the use of drugs, typically to trigger sexual arousal, increase sexual pleasure, and/or facilitate sexual encounters that last several hours or days.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001267","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000399","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001235"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001267"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:m