rculation publications usually reproduced via photocopier; use for zines created by non-binary people and/or focusing on non-binary identities, issues, or culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000965","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001132"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003153","dc:identifier":"homoit0003153","skos:prefLabel":"Two-Spirit zines","skos:altLabel":["2S zines","Two Spirit zines","Two Spirited zines","Two-Spirited zines"],"rdfs:comment":"Independent, small-circulation publications usually reproduced via photocopier; use for zines created by Two-Spirit people and/or focusing on Two-Spirit identities, issues, or culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002719","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000965","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002719"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003154","dc:identifier":"homoit0003154","skos:prefLabel":"Queer zines","rdfs:comment":"Independent, small-circulation publications usually reproduced via photocopier; use for zines created by queer people and/or focusing on queer identity, issues, or cultures.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000965","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001200"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001132"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003155","dc:identifier":"homoit0003155","skos:prefLabel":"Lesbian zines","rdfs:comment":"Independent, small-circulation publications usually reproduced via photocopier; use for zines created by lesbians and/or focusing on lesbian identity, issues, or culture.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000766","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000965"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001132"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003156","dc:identifier":"homoit0003156","skos:prefLabel":"Gay zines","rdfs:comment":"Independent, small-circulation publications usually reproduced via photocopier; use for zines created by gay people and/or focusing on gay identity, issues, or culture.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000521","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000965"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001132"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003157","dc:identifier":"homoit0003157","skos:prefLabel":"Trans-exclusionary radical feminists","skos:altLabel":["Gender critical feminists","TERFs","Trans-exclusionary feminist"],"rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to a transphobic and transantagonistic ideology that rejects trans and gender diverse identities and rights, and believes that recognition of these identities and rights constitutes discrimination and oppression towards cisgender women. Though originally considered a fringe offshoot of feminism, trans-exclusionary radical feminist groups have formed alliances with right-wing, far-right extremists, and anti-feminist organizations in order to spread misinformation and further anti-trans sentiment and legislation. Use when resources are about trans-exclusionary radical feminists or when an individual identifies as such. ","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003158"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003157"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003158","dc:identifier":"homoit0003158","skos:prefLabel":"Trans-exclusionary radical feminism","skos:altLabel":["Gender critical feminism","TERF ideology","Trans-exclusionary feminism"],"rdfs:comment":"A transphobic and transantagonistic ideology that rejects trans and gender diverse identities and rights, and believes that recognition of these identities and rights constitutes discrimination and oppression towards cisgender women. Though originally considered a fringe offshoot of feminism, trans-exclusionary radical feminist groups have formed alliances with right-wing, far-right extremists, and anti-feminist organizations in order to spread misinformation and further anti-trans sentiment and legislation. ","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000115","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000565","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001467","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001892"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000062","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000437","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001260","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001885","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003157","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003737"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-02"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003159","dc:identifier":"homoit0003159","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ country music","rdfs:comment":"Music expressing a LGBTQ+ sensibility, produced within the larger country genre since the 1930s.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003610","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003160","dc:identifier":"homoit0003160","skos:prefLabel":"Drag in film","skos:altLabel":["Drag in cinema","Drag in movies"],"rdfs:comment":"Films with significant characters who appear in drag. Not to be confused with films where a principal actor plays a character who identifies as a gender other than what the actor identifies as.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000367","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002327"],"skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000249","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000318"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003161","dc:identifier":"homoit0003161","skos:prefLabel":"Gay musicals","skos:altLabel":"Homosexual musicals","rdfs:comment":"Musicals created by gay directors, depicting gay men, or that are regarded as important within gay culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001031","skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98001886"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003162","dc:identifier":"homoit0003162","skos:prefLabel":"Bisexual musicals","rdfs:comment":"Musicals created by bisexual directors, depicting bisexual individuals, or that are regarded as important within bisexual culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001031","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003163","dc:identifier":"homoit0003163","skos:prefLabel":"Transgender musicals","rdfs:comment":"Musicals created by transgender directors, depicting transgender individuals, or that are regarded as important within transgender culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001031","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003164","dc:identifier":"homoit0003164","skos:prefLabel":"Asexual musicals","rdfs:comment":"Musicals created by asexual directors, depicting asexual individuals, or that are regarded as important within asexual culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001031","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003165","dc:identifier":"homoit0003165","skos:prefLabel":"Intersex musicals","rdfs:comment":"Musicals created by intersex directors, depicting intersex individuals, or that are regarded as important within intersex culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001031","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003166","dc:identifier":"homoit0003166","skos:prefLabel":"Lesbian operas","rdfs:comment":"Operas created by lesbian directors, depicting lesbian individuals, or that are regarded as important within lesbian culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002886","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000755","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003167","dc:identifier":"homoit0003167","skos:prefLabel":"Queer operas","rdfs:comment":"Operas created by queer directors, depicting queer individuals, or that are regarded as important within queer culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002886","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003168","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003168","dc:identifier":"homoit0003168","skos:prefLabel":"Two-Spirit operas","skos:altLabel":["2S operas","Two Spirit operas","Two Spirited operas","Two-Spirited operas"],"rdfs:comment":"Operas created by Two-Spirit directors, depicting Two-Spirit individuals, or that are regarded as important within Two-Spirit culture.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002886","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002889","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002891","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003167"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003168"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-09"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003169","dc:identifier":"homoit0003169","skos:prefLabel":"Lesbian feminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to lesbian feminism, an ideology that encourages women to focus their efforts, activities, and relationships toward other women rather than men, often advocating for lesbianism as the logical result of feminism. Use when resources are about lesbian feminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000741","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000753"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh93000705"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003170","dc:identifier":"homoit0003170","skos:prefLabel":"Black feminists","skos:altLabel":["Afro feminists","Afro-feminists"],"rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to a form of feminism that developed in response to the failures of mainstream feminist and civil rights efforts to acknowledge the ways white supremacy and the patriarchy interact to inform the particular experiences of Black women. Use when resources are about Black feminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002270","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003176"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003171","dc:identifier":"homoit0003171","skos:prefLabel":"Eco-feminists","skos:altLabel":"Ecofeminsts","rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to the political and philosophical movement that views feminism and concerns for the environment as inherently related. Use when resources are about eco-feminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000387","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003172","dc:identifier":"homoit0003172","skos:prefLabel":"First-wave feminists","skos:altLabel":"First wave feminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who was part of a period of women's rights activism in the 19th and early 20th centuries that was primarily focused on legal rights such as women's right to vote. Use when resources are about first-wave feminists.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000444","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003173","dc:identifier":"homoit0003173","skos:prefLabel":"Second-wave feminists","skos:altLabel":"Second wave feminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who was part of or subscribes to beliefs developed during a period of feminist political activity (also referred to as women’s liberation) beginning in the early 1960s that critiqued male-dominated institutions and cultural practices in society. Use when resources are about second-wave feminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001260","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003174","dc:identifier":"homoit0003174","skos:prefLabel":"Third-wave feminists","skos:altLabel":"Third wave feminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who was part of or subscribes to beliefs developed during a period of feminist political activity beginning in the early 1990s that embraced diversity and individualism in women and sought to redefine what it meant to be a feminist. The third-wave is characterized by the emergence of new feminist movements and theories such as intersectionality, sex positivity, ecofeminism, transfeminism, and postmodern feminism. Use when resources are about third-wave feminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002275","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003175","dc:identifier":"homoit0003175","skos:prefLabel":"Transfeminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who is part of or subscribes to beliefs developed as part of a movement by and for trans woman who view the liberation of trans women as essential to the liberation of all women. Use when resources are about transfeminists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002274","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003176","dc:identifier":"homoit0003176","skos:prefLabel":"Womanists","rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to womanism, an ideology that grew out of the perceived indifference of the feminist movement towards the needs of Black women, who are often excluded from the categories of \"female\" and \"femininity\" as understood by white feminists. At the core of womanism is the idea that mainstream feminism is a movement led by white women to serve white women's goals, which can be indifferent or even oppositional to the needs of Black women. Use for resources about womanists or when an individual identifies as such.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002272","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003170"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003176"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003177","dc:identifier":"homoit0003177","skos:prefLabel":"Radical feminists","rdfs:comment":"A person who subscribes to a perspective within feminism that calls for a radical reordering of society in which male supremacy is eliminated in all social and economic contexts. Distinct from and not to be confused with trans-exclusionary radical feminists. Use for resources about radical feminists or for individuals who identify as such, unless trans-exclusionary radical feminists is a more appropriate term.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000439","skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003766","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001230","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000439"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003178","dc:identifier":"homoit0003178","skos:prefLabel":"Masks (Erotic)","rdfs:comment":"Masks worn as a fetish fashion accessory or for sensual or sexual play.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001266","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003066"],"skos:narrower":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003112","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003083","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001266"},"dc:issued":{"@t