tates. Do not conflate with Muslim people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003382","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003390","dc:identifier":"homoit0003390","skos:prefLabel":"Arab American intersex people","skos:altLabel":["Intersex Arab American people","Intersex Arab Americans"],"rdfs:comment":"Intersex people who are descended from Arab peoples and were born in the United States, or intersex people born in Arab countries who live in or have a strong connection to the United States. Do not conflate with Muslim people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003382","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003391","dc:identifier":"homoit0003391","skos:prefLabel":"Arab American aromantic people","skos:altLabel":["Aromantic Arab American people","Aromantic Arab Americans"],"rdfs:comment":"Aromantic people who are descended from Arab peoples and were born in the United States, or aromantic people born in Arab countries who live in or have a strong connection to the United States. Do not conflate with Muslim people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003382","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003392","dc:identifier":"homoit0003392","skos:prefLabel":"Arab aromantic people","skos:altLabel":["Aromantic Arab people","Aromantic Arabs"],"rdfs:comment":"Aromantic people who are from Arab countries and/or are descended from Arab peoples. Do not conflate with Muslim people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002009","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003393","dc:identifier":"homoit0003393","skos:prefLabel":"Aboriginal Australian non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Non-binary Aboriginal Australian people","Non-binary Aboriginal Australians","Nonbinary Aboriginal Australian people","Nonbinary Aboriginal Australians"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to one or more of the various Indigenous peoples of Australia; do not use to refer to the Indigenous people of the Torres Strait Islands, who are considered ethnically and culturally distinct. Only use to describe people who identify as Aboriginal Australian.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000002","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003394","dc:identifier":"homoit0003394","skos:prefLabel":"Assamese non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Non-binary Asomiya","Non-binary Assamese people","Nonbinary Asomiya","Nonbinary Assamese people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are a part of the socio-ethnic Assamese peoples, speak the Assamese language, or reside in the Indian state of Assam.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002060","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003395","dc:identifier":"homoit0003395","skos:prefLabel":"Awadhi non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Non-binary Awadhi people","Non-binary Awadhis","Nonbinary Awadhi people","Nonbinary Awadhis"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who speak the Awadhi dialect and reside in or are descended from those who resided in the Awadh region of Uttar Pradesh.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002070","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003396","dc:identifier":"homoit0003396","skos:prefLabel":"Bengali non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Non-binary Bengali people","Non-binary Bengalis","Nonbinary Bengali people","Nonbinary Bengalis"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who speak the Bengali language or are of Bengali descent. ","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002086","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003397","dc:identifier":"homoit0003397","skos:prefLabel":"Bhil non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Bheel non-binary people","Bheel nonbinary people","Non-binary Bhils","Nonbinary Bhils"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who speak the Bhil language and belong to or are descended from the Bhil tribal group.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002094","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003398","dc:identifier":"homoit0003398","skos:prefLabel":"Bhojpuri non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Non-binary Bhojpuri people","Non-binary Bhojpuriyas","Nonbinary Bhojpuri people","Nonbinary Bhojpuriyas"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who speak the Bhojpuri language and live in or are descended from those who inhabited the Bhojpuri-Purvanchal region of India and Nepal.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002078","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003399","dc:identifier":"homoit0003399","skos:prefLabel":"Biracial non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Bi-racial non-binary people","Bi-racial nonbinary people","Non-binary bi-racial people","Non-binary biracial people","Nonbinary bi-racial people","Nonbinary biracial people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to two or more racial groups. Only use to describe people who self-identify as biracial.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000820","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003400","dc:identifier":"homoit0003400","skos:prefLabel":"Black non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Black nonbinary people","Non-binary Black people","Nonbinary Black people"],"rdfs:comment":"Black people who are non-binary. Use only for individuals who self-identity as Black. Follow the individual’s preference for African American or Black whenever possible.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000208","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003401","dc:identifier":"homoit0003401","skos:prefLabel":"Chakma non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Chakma nonbinary people","Non-binary Chakma people","Nonbinary Chakma people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to or are descended from the Chakma tribal group.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002102","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003402","dc:identifier":"homoit0003402","skos:prefLabel":"Chicano/a/x non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Chicana non-binary people","Chicano non-binary people","Chicanx non-binary people","Non-binary Chicanas","Non-binary Chicanos","Non-binary Chicanx people","Nonbinary Chicanas","Nonbinary Chicanos","Nonbinary Chicanx people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people of Mexican descent born in the United States; only use to describe people who self-identify as Chicano, Chicana, or Chicanx. Do not conflate with Latino/a/x or Hispanic people.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002007","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003403","dc:identifier":"homoit0003403","skos:prefLabel":"Closeted non-binary people","skos:altLabel":"Closeted nonbinary people","rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who do not identify as such to others.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001783","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003404","dc:identifier":"homoit0003404","skos:prefLabel":"Daughters of non-binary people","skos:altLabel":"Daughters of nonbinary people","rdfs:comment":"Daughters who have one or more non-binary parent.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002352","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003405","dc:identifier":"homoit0003405","skos:prefLabel":"Dogra non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Dogra nonbinary people","Non-binary Dogra people","Non-binary Dogras","Nonbinary Dogra people","Nonbinary Dogras"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are of the Dogra people of India and Pakistan and speak the Dogri language.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002126","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003406","dc:identifier":"homoit0003406","skos:prefLabel":"Fathers of non-binary people","skos:altLabel":"Fathers of nonbinary people","rdfs:comment":"People who assume the role of father to non-binary people. Only use to describe individuals who identify as fathers.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002342","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003407","dc:identifier":"homoit0003407","skos:prefLabel":"Garhwali non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Garhwali nonbinary people","Non-binary Garhwali people","Non-binary Garhwalis","Nonbinary Garhwali people","Nonbinary Garhwalis"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to or are descended from those native to Garhwal in Uttarakhand and who speak Garhwali.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002134","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003408","dc:identifier":"homoit0003408","skos:prefLabel":"Gujarati non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Gujarati nonbinary people","Non-binary Gujarati people","Non-binary Gujaratis","Nonbinary Gujarati people","Nonbinary Gujaratis"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who reside in or are descended from those indigenous to the Indian state of Gujarat.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002231","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003409","dc:identifier":"homoit0003409","skos:prefLabel":"Haryanvi non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Haryanvi nonbinary people","Non-binary Haryanvi people","Non-binary Haryanvis","Nonbinary Haryanvi people","Nonbinary Haryanvis"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are indigenous to or descended from those indigenous to what is now the Indian state of Haryana. This term can also apply to those who currently reside in Haryana.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002239","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003410","dc:identifier":"homoit0003410","skos:prefLabel":"Inuit non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Inuit nonbinary people","Non-binary Inuit people","Non-binary Inuit","Nonbinary Inuit people","Nonbinary Inuit"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are Inuit, or part of several Indigenous peoples inhabiting the Inuit homeland in the Arctic and subarctic regions of Greenland, Canada, and Alaska. Only use for people who identify as Inuit.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000676","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003411","dc:identifier":"homoit0003411","skos:prefLabel":"Jewish non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Jewish nonbinary people","Non-binary Jewish people","Non-binary Jews","Nonbinary Jewish people","Nonbinary Jews"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are Jewish.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000682","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003412","dc:identifier":"homoit0003412","skos:prefLabel":"Kalash non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Kalash nonbinary people","Non-binary Kalash people","Non-binary Kalasha","Nonbinary Kalash people","Nonbinary Kalasha"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to the indigenous Kalasha people and reside in the Chitral District of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa province in Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002247","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003413","dc:identifier":"homoit0003413","skos:prefLabel":"Kānaka Maoli non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Kanaka Maoli non-binary people","Kanaka Maoli nonbinary people","Kānaka Maoli nonbinary people","Non-binary Kanaka Maoli","Non-binary Kānaka Maoli","Nonbinary Kanaka Maoli","Nonbinary Kānaka Maoli"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are part of the Indigenous people of Mokupuni o Hawai‘i, or the Hawaiian Islands; only use to refer to people who identify as Kanaka Maoli.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001955","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003414","dc:identifier":"homoit0003414","skos:prefLabel":"Kashmiri non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Kashmiri nonbinary people","Non-binary Kashmiri people","Non-binary Kashmiris","Nonbinary Kashmiri people","Nonbinary Kashmiris"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who live in or are descended from those native to the Kashmir Valley in the Indian subcontinent.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002295","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003415","dc:identifier":"homoit0003415","skos:prefLabel":"Kho non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Chitrali non-binary people","Chitrali nonbinary people","Kho nonbinary people","Non-binary Kho people","Nonbinary Kho people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to or are descended from the people indigenous to the Chitral and Ghizer districts of modern-day Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002110","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003416","dc:identifier":"homoit0003416","skos:prefLabel":"Konkan non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Konkan nonbinary people","Non-binary Konkani people","Non-binary Konkani","Nonbinary Konkani people","Nonbinary Konkani"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are from or descended from those native to the Konkan region of the Indian subcontinent, and who speak any of the dialects of the Konkani language.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002303","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003417","dc:identifier":"homoit0003417","skos:prefLabel":"Kumaoni non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Kumain non-binary people","Kumain nonbinary people","Kumaiye non-binary people","Kumaiye nonbinary people","Kumaoni nonbinary people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who live mostly in Kumaon region in the Indian Himalayas. They might also speak the Kumaoni language as their first language.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002311","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003418","dc:identifier":"homoit0003418","skos:prefLabel":"Kutchi non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Kutchi nonbinary people","Non-binary Kutchi people","Nonbinary Kutchi people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who are from or are descended from those native to the Kutch district of the Indian state of Gujarat and the Sindh region of Pakistan.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002319","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003419","dc:identifier":"homoit0003419","skos:prefLabel":"Latino/a/x non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Latina non-binary people","Latina nonbinary people","Latino non-binary people","Latino nonbinary people","Latino/a/x nonbinary people","Latinx non-binary people","Latinx nonbinary people","Non-binary Latinas","Non-binary Latino/a/x people","Non-binary Latinos","Non-binary Latinx","Nonbinary Latinas","Nonbinary Latino/a/x people","Nonbinary Latinos","Nonbinary Latinx"],"rdfs:comment":"Latin American people who are non-binary; only use to describe individuals who self-identify as Latino, Latina, or Latinx. Do not conflate with Chicano/a/x or Hispanic.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000253","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003420","dc:identifier":"homoit0003420","skos:prefLabel":"Maldivian non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["Dhivehin non-binary people","Dhivehin nonbinary people","Maldivian nonbinary people","Non-binary Maldivians","Nonbinary Maldivians"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to or are descended from the people native to the Maldives (including the island of Minicoy) and speak the Maldivian language.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002118","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003421","dc:identifier":"homoit0003421","skos:prefLabel":"Multiracial non-binary people","skos:altLabel":[" Non-binary muti-racial people","Multi-racial nonbinary people","Multiracial nonbinary people","Muti-racial non-binary people","Non-binary multiracial people","Nonbinary multi-racial people","Nonbinary multiracial people"],"rdfs:comment":"Non-binary people who belong to two or more racial groups.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000903","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003422","dc:identifier":"homoit0003422","skos:prefLabel":"Native American non-binary people","skos:altLabel":["American Indian non-binary people","American Indian nonbinary people","Native American nonbinary people","Non-binary American Indians","Non-binary Native Americans","Nonbinary American Indians","Nonbinary Native Americans"],"rdfs:comment":"People who are part of the Native peoples of the continental United States and Canada (excluding Inuit people) and self-identity as Non-binary. Do not conflate with Two-Spirit people. Use more specific terms when available.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001037","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-07-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://ho