nts","rdfs:comment":"Organized public or social occasions for megasexual people and communities.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000861"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003608","dc:identifier":"homoit0003608","skos:prefLabel":"Black queer archives","skos:altLabel":"Queer Black archives","rdfs:comment":"Collections of records and materials relating to Black queer people and communities, or collections of records and materials relating to Black people and communities that are curated, organized, and presented from a queer perspective. Can include a variety of organizations and institutions from community to government archives.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000066","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001163","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001755"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003609","dc:identifier":"homoit0003609","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+-affirming religious services","skos:altLabel":["LGBTQ+ affirming religious services","LGBTQ+ religious services","Religious services (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Religious services, or gatherings of people belonging to the same religious group or belief system, that are accepting and supportive of LGBTQ+ people and their identities. Includes services specifically intended for LGBTQ+ people within a denomination or sect that is otherwise not LGBTQ+-affirming.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000530","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000928"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003609"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003610","dc:identifier":"homoit0003610","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ music","skos:altLabel":"Music (LGBTQ)","rdfs:comment":"Music created by LGBTQ+ artists, for LGBTQ+ audiences, and/or that expresses an LGBTQ+ sensibility.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000816","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003159","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003611","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003612"],"skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000908","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003611","dc:identifier":"homoit0003611","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ rap music","skos:altLabel":["Rap music (LGBTQ)","Rap (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Rap music created by LGBTQ+ artists, for LGBTQ+ audiences, and/or that expresses an LGBTQ+ sensibility.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003610","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003612","dc:identifier":"homoit0003612","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ pop music","skos:altLabel":["Pop music (LGBTQ)","Pop (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ+ popular music","Popular music (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Pop music created by LGBTQ+ artists, for LGBTQ+ audiences, and/or that expresses an LGBTQ+ sensibility.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003610","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003613","dc:identifier":"homoit0003613","skos:prefLabel":"Women's sexuality","skos:altLabel":"Female sexuality","rdfs:comment":"Term used to describe the ways in which women experience and express themselves sexually, including the types of people and practices they are sexually interested in.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001306","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002279","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001510"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001306"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003614","dc:identifier":"homoit0003614","skos:prefLabel":"Queer architecture","skos:altLabel":"Queer design","rdfs:comment":"A school of architecture that seeks to create spaces that critique normative conceptions of gender and sexuality.","skos:broader":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002601","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001219"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003615","dc:identifier":"homoit0003615","skos:prefLabel":"Queer ecology","skos:altLabel":"Queer ecologies","rdfs:comment":"A school of ecology that seeks to understand nature, biology, and sexuality through the framing of queer theory. Queer ecology rejects the presumption of heterosexuality and cisgenderedness as natural, as well as notions of human exceptionalism and anthropocentrism.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001219","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003616","dc:identifier":"homoit0003616","skos:prefLabel":"Decolonial theory","skos:altLabel":["Decoloniality","Decolonizing theory","Postcolonial theory","Postcolonialism"],"rdfs:comment":"A school of thought that rejects Eurocentric knowledge hierarchies and ways of being, including the presumed superiority of white Western culture.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001365","skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh97007835"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003618","dc:identifier":"homoit0003618","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ librarians","skos:altLabel":"Librarians (LGBTQ+)","rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people, typically with degrees in library science, who work, manage, or assist in a library setting.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003617","skos:narrower":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003620","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003621","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003622","http