ic television personalities","skos:altLabel":"Greyromantic TV personalities","rdfs:comment":"Greyromantic people who are well-known to the public through their appearances on television shows, typically as themselves rather than in scripted roles.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003677","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003690","dc:identifier":"homoit0003690","skos:prefLabel":"Megasexual television personalities","skos:altLabel":"Megasexual TV personalities","rdfs:comment":"Megasexual people who are well-known to the public through their appearances on television shows, typically as themselves rather than in scripted roles.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003677","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003691","dc:identifier":"homoit0003691","skos:prefLabel":"Gentrification","rdfs:comment":"A process of economic and demographic change within a historically disinvested neighborhood by means of real estate investment and an influx of new, higher-income residents, typically resulting in the displacement of long-time, lower-income residents.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000356","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002257","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003140","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003692"],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85053952"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003691"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003692","dc:identifier":"homoit0003692","skos:prefLabel":"Redlining","skos:altLabel":["Red lining","Credit card redlining"],"rdfs:comment":"A discriminatory practice in which financial services are withheld from neighborhoods that have significant numbers of racial and ethnic minorities. Redlining includes but is not limited to denial of credit, insurance, and healthcare; inflated mortgage and interest rates; and the development of food deserts. The term has its roots in the New Deal when color-coded maps were made of metropolitan areas in the United States to indicate where it was considered safe to insure mortgages. Black neighborhoods and surrounding areas were colored red to indicate mortgages should not be insured there.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002257","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003691"],"skos:closeMatch":[{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85038399"},{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85038383"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003692"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003693","dc:identifier":"homoit0003693","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ safe spaces","skos:altLabel":["Safe spaces (LGBTQ)","Safe places (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ+ safe places","LGBTQ+ safe zones","Safe zones (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Public spaces designated as safe for, or accepting and affirming of, LGBTQ+ people, often by allies. LGBTQ+ safe spaces are sometimes identified through the display of stickers or placards.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003699","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000038","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000538","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000873"],"skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2023000011"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000900"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003694","dc:identifier":"homoit0003694","skos:prefLabel":"Impact of COVID-19 pandemic on LGBTQ+ people","skos:altLabel":["COVID-19 pandemic impact on LGBTQ+ people","Impact of pandemic on LGBTQ+ people","Pandemic impact on LGBTQ+ people","COVID-19 pandemic and LGBTQ+ people","COVID-19 and LGBTQ+ people"],"rdfs:comment":"The particular impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on LGBTQ+ people and communities, including changes in access to health care, intimate relationship dynamics and safer sex practices, financial stability, social connectedness, and mental health.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000614","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000947"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003694"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-23"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003695","dc:identifier":"homoit0003695","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ philanthropy","skos:altLabel":["Philanthropy (LGBTQ)","LGBTQ+ charity","Charity (LGBTQ)"],"rdfs:comment":"Efforts to improve the welfare of LGBTQ+ people and communities, especially by the donation of money or resources to charitable causes.","skos:related":["https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001026","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000006","https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003696"],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003695"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-23"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003696","dc:identifier":"homoit0003696","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ philanthropists","skos:altLabel":"Philanthropists (LGBTQ)","rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people who seek to improve the welfare of others, especially by the donation of money or resources to charitable causes.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003695","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-23"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003697","dc:identifier":"homoit0003697","skos:prefLabel":"LGBTQ+ punks","skos:altLabel":"Punks (LGBTQ)","rdfs:comment":"LGBTQ+ people involved in the punk community, which originated in the 1970s with punk rock music and is now associated with various music subgenres, fashions, and ideologies.","skos:broader":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915","skos:related":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003698","skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-23"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-02-23"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"},"skos:changeNote":"Version 3.7.0"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003698","dc:identifier":"homoit0003698","skos:prefLa